: A Memory-Efficient Full-Parameter Optimization of Large Language Models' — NOT verified from primary source in this workspace.", "Per-step 'learning perturbation' is the parameter-difference Δθ_t = θ_{t+1} − θ_t at the optimizer boundary (post-step), not the raw gradient and not the post-LR-scaled direction.", "'Heavy-tailed singular value distribution' is operationalised as a Pareto(α) fit on the upper tail with α estimated by Hill estimator and a KS goodness-of-fit; a heavy tail is positive if α ∈ (0, 2] (variance possibly infinite) AND Marchenko–Pastur reference is rejected.", "'Effective rank' defaults to Roy & Vetterli (2007); numerical-rank @ ε is a secondary cross-check.", "Comparable-by-default thresholds τ_e = 0.20 and d_e = 0.30 are PLACEHOLDERS, to be pre-registered with the researcher at the result stage."], "uncertainties": ["Exact BAdam update rule, default block size, LR scaling, and state-allocation strategy are assumed, not source-confirmed.", "Whether the sandbox will allow execution at all (no GPU, no installed ML stack, no network); this prototype of the design accommodates that by being deliverable as a design protocol.", "Whether task.json's referenced track.md carries additional scoping constraints that I cannot see here.", "Whether 'heavy-tailed' admits α > 2 in this paper's convention is unknown; threshold to be agreed.", "Whether the per-step or per-cycle ΔW is the right primary endpoint for comparing erank is a definitional call, not a statistical one."], "kind": "ReviewHandoffAction"}, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "call-b096fc49-352e-4a8c-8014-d3a7e2f6651c", "tool_call": {"id": "call-b096fc49-352e-4a8c-8014-d3a7e2f6651c", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{\"summary\": \"Propose staged plan for BAdam vs Adam spectral-diagnostic experiment\", \"stage\": \"plan\", \"answer\": \"```json\\n{\\n  \\\"approach\\\": {\\n    \\\"restated_question\\\": \\\"Does the per-step learning perturbation \\u0394\\u03b8_t produced by BAdam, when decomposed by transformer module, show (a) a heavy-tailed singular-value spectrum and (b) an effective rank comparable to Adam's, during finetuning?\\\",\\n    \\\"design_summary\\\": \\\"A paired, module-stratified, multi-seed spectral-diagnostic study. Two optimizers (Adam vs BAdam) are run side-by-side on identical init weights, identical data-ordering, identical LR schedule, with the optimizer rule as the only varying factor. Per-step \\u0394W = (\\u03b8_after_optimizer_step \\u2212 \\u03b8_before_optimizer_step) is captured at the optimizer boundary for every tracked module. Each captured \\u0394W is then characterised by (i) its SVD singular values \\u03c3_i; (ii) effective rank by Roy\\u2013Vetterli (and a numerical-rank threshold as a robustness cross-check); (iii) heavy-tail signature via Hill tail-exponent \\u03b1 and a KS goodness-of-fit of the upper tail against Pareto vs Marchenko\\u2013Pastur. Module-stratified paired Wilcoxon + Cohen's d + bootstrapped CIs decide 'comparable'.\\\",\\n    \\\"conditions\\\": [\\n      \\\"C1 Adam \\u2014 full-parameter, default AdamW with \\u03b21, \\u03b22, \\u03b5, decoupled weight decay; gold reference.\\\",\\n      \\\"C2 BAdam \\u2014 paper-default configuration (block count TBD; see consequential choices).\\\",\\n      \\\"C3 BAdam-scan \\u2014 block-size sensitivity sweep (e.g., T \\u2208 {2, 4, 8, 16, 32}) to test robustness of the claim.\\\",\\n      \\\"C4 LoRA \\u2014 known low-rank perturbation baseline (rank \\u2208 {8, 16, 32}); control for what Adam-grade spectrum 'should' look like.\\\",\\n      \\\"C5 SGD \\u2014 checks that any structural effect is Adam-attributable vs gradient-attributable.\\\",\\n      \\\"Optional bench C6: GaLore \\u2014 if researcher wants a richer comparator.\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"modules_tracked\\\": [\\\"q_proj\\\", \\\"k_proj\\\", \\\"v_proj\\\", \\\"o_proj\\\", \\\"gate_proj\\\", \\\"up_proj\\\", \\\"down_proj\\\", \\\"embed_tokens\\\", \\\"lm_head\\\"],\\n    \\\"diagnostics_per_update\\\": [\\n      \\\"Truncated SVD; m = min(in_dim, out_dim).\\\",\\n      \\\"Effective rank erank_RV = exp(-\\u03a3 p_i log p_i) where p_i = \\u03c3_i / \\u2016\\u03c3\\u2016_1.\\\",\\n      \\\"Numerical rank at \\u03b5 \\u2208 {1e-3, 1e-2, 1e-1} \\u00b7 \\u03c3_max.\\\",\\n      \\\"Concentration ratios: top-1/total, top-10/total, top-10%/total.\\\",\\n      \\\"Hill tail-exponent \\u03b1\\u0302 on top k = \\u2308\\u221am\\u2309 \\u03c3_i; cross-checked with MLE Pareto.\\\",\\n      \\\"Goodness-of-fit: KS (Pareto vs \\u03c3_i) and KS (Marchenko\\u2013Pastur reference).\\\",\\n      \\\"Log-log spectrum plot (per-condition, per-module) for shape inspection.\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"decision_rule_for_comparable\\\": {\\n      \\\"erank_comparable_if\\\": \\\"module-level |median(\\u0394_erank)|/median(erank_Adam) < \\u03c4_e and |Cohen's d| < d_e (defaults \\u03c4_e=0.20, d_e=0.30 \\u2014 to be pre-registered at result stage).\\\",\\n      \\\"tail_comparable_if\\\": \\\"\\u03b1_BAdam \\u2208 \\u03b1_Adam \\u00b1 2\\u00b7SE_Hill AND both conditions reject Marchenko\\u2013Pastur (heavy-tailedness preserved in both optimizers).\\\",\\n      \\\"multiple_comparison_correction\\\": \\\"Holm across the 9 tracked modules.\\\",\\n      \\\"per_step_vs_per_cycle\\\": \\\"Two complementary views: (a) per-step \\u0394W (BAdam active block only); (b) cycle-aggregated \\u0394W over T steps compared to Adam's same-window \\u0394W. Pre-register which is the primary endpoint.\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"controls_and_pairing\\\": [\\n      \\\"Identical init \\u03b8_0 across conditions.\\\",\\n      \\\"Pre-generated, cached token stream (deterministic sample order).\\\",\\n      \\\"Identical LR schedule (e.g., cosine to 0 with linear warmup).\\\",\\n      \\\"Identical micro-batch composition.\\\",\\n      \\\"Adam moments (m, v) and BAdam block-scheduler state both re-initialised identically at step 0.\\\",\\n      \\\"\\u22653 seeds per condition; results aggregated with bootstrap CIs.\\\",\\n      \\\"Snapshot hook ONLY at the optimizer boundary (post-step), so \\u0394W is the actual committed update, not the gradient or pre-step LR-adjusted direction.\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"feasibility_checks_before_heavy_runs\\\": [\\n      \\\"SVD pipeline: rank-1 analytic matrix \\u2192 erank \\u2248 1; isotropic \\u0394W \\u2192 erank \\u2248 m.\\\",\\n      \\\"Heavy-tail synthetic: \\u03c3_i ~ Pareto(\\u03b1=1.5) \\u2192 \\u03b1\\u0302 within bootstrap CI of 1.5.\\\",\\n      \\\"Light-tail synthetic: \\u03c3_i from i.i.d. Gaussian random matrix \\u2192 MP not rejected; Pareto rejected.\\\",\\n      \\\"Round-trip on a 2-layer CPU transformer: optimiser-step \\u0394W equals (\\u03b8_after \\u2212 \\u03b8_before) for both Adam and BAdam.\\\",\\n      \\\"Numerics: detect near-zero \\u03c3_i floor (early steps when few params have moved) and apply pre-registered trim rule before Hill estimation.\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"compute_and_scope\\\": [\\n      \\\"Local sandbox has no GPU, no installed ML stack (torch/scipy/numpy/transformers absent), and network is disabled.\\\",\\n      \\\"task.json says repositories and compute are not required for design-only.\\\",\\n      \\\"Therefore, the experiment described above is a protocol to be executed on an external GPU host; this design only delivers the design artifacts.\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"deferred_to_result_stage\\\": [\\n      \\\"Exact BAdam block-size grid and LR scaling.\\\",\\n      \\\"Number of steps N and pilot calibration curve (N \\u2208 {100, 500, 2000}) to find metric-stabilisation regime.\\\",\\n      \\\"Pre-registered thresholds \\u03c4_e, d_e with researcher.\\\",\\n      \\\"Reporting template (per-module table: erank, d_erank, \\u03b1, KS p-values, spectra plot grid).\\\"\\n    ]\\n  },\\n  \\\"consequential_choices\\\": [\\n    \\\"C1. Source of BAdam: implement from paper spec vs pin to a specific commit of a public repo; reproducibility matters at execution time.\\\",\\n    \\\"C2. Base model: Llama-2-7B / Llama-3.1-8B / Qwen-2.5-7B / Phi-3-mini (smaller = cheaper but less standard for BAdam claims).\\\",\\n    \\\"C3. BAdam block configuration: deterministic contiguous partition vs V-BAdam random-per-step; default block count.\\\",\\n    \\\"C4. Comparison set: just Adam-BAdam, or include LoRA / GaLore / SGD as auxiliary baselines.\\\",\\n    \\\"C5. LR scaling rule for BAdam's active block (Adam LR \\u00d7 1 vs Adam LR \\u00d7 T effective) \\u2014 changes \\u0394W magnitude materially.\\\",\\n    \\\"C6. Dataset & task: Alpaca-style instruction vs GLUE classification \\u2014 different gradient spectra.\\\",\\n    \\\"C7. Number of steps N and seed count S (power analysis to be done in result stage).\\\",\\n    \\\"C8. Effective-rank definition: Roy\\u2013Vetterli only vs paired with numerical-rank threshold; pre-register which is primary.\\\",\\n    \\\"C9. Pre-registered thresholds (\\u03c4_e, d_e) for 'comparable' equivalence bounds.\\\",\\n    \\\"C10. Whether per-step or per-cycle \\u0394W is the primary endpoint \\u2014 a definitional choice, not a statistical one.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"uncertainties\\\": [\\n    \\\"No source artifacts in /workspace: only task.json is present. The BAdam paper, code, default hyper-parameters, and the upstream reference implementation are NOT available locally and network is disabled. I treat BAdam's exact update rule and default configuration as ASSUMPTION \\u2014 to be re-verified from primary source at execution time.\\\",\\n    \\\"'Heavy-tailed' has no single canonical threshold in the literature; common practice is \\u03b1 \\u2264 2 (Pareto-tail variance infinite) for 'heavy'. A pre-registered definition must be agreed.\\\",\\n    \\\"BAdam by construction updates only 1/T of params per step, so per-step erank is biased low relative to Adam by construction. The 'aggregate over a full cycle' view is the fairer spectral comparison; both perceptions must be disclosed.\\\",\\n    \\\"Numerical instability of SVD on low-magnitude \\u0394Ws in early steps may bias Hill estimation; a trim rule must be specified.\\\",\\n    \\\"task.json references documents/track.md but the file is not present in the workspace; unknown whether it imposes additional scoping.\\\",\\n    \\\"GPU is absent in the sandbox; spectral measurement code itself is CPU-cheap, but generating the upstream updates is GPU-bound and out of scope here.\\\",\\n    \\\"Adam's \\u03b21/\\u03b22/weight-decay interaction with BAdam's per-step block rotation is not specified in my current information \\u2014 must be sourced.\\\",\\n    \\\"Whether BAdam stores optimizer state per-block or globally materially changes spectral properties of \\u0394W across steps; unverifiable here.\\\",\\n    \\\"Definition of 'effective rank comparable' is intrinsically scale-and-bias sensitive; an explicit test family and thresholds must be agreed before numbers are analysed (result-stage deliverable).\\\"\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\", \"evidence\": \"Workspace inspection: /workspace contains exactly one file, /workspace/task.json. task.json's documents field references 'track.md' but track.md is absent in the workspace. The full pip list and find scan turned up no BAdam/Adam/HuggingFace code, no checkpoints, no dataset files. Python 3.12 is available but torch, scipy, numpy, and transformers are not installed (verified via `python -c 'import X'` \\u2014 all failed with ModuleNotFoundError). `nvidia-smi` reports 'NVIDIA-SMI has failed because it couldn't communicate with the NVIDIA driver' \\u2014 confirming no GPU in the sandbox. A probe to https://huggingface.co returned HTTP 000 within a 2-second timeout, confirming network is disabled. 24 CPU cores, 125 GiB RAM, 1.8 TB disk are available. task.json explicitly states 'Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required', matching the design-only framing of this turn. Taken together: no source artifacts and no execution substrate, so the only honest deliverable is a design protocol plus an explicit list of researcher-decision points and an explicit list of uncertainties.\", \"assumptions\": [\"Pretrained model weights and BAdam reference implementation are not available in /workspace and cannot be fetched (no network, no installed stack); any execution would require external resources at the next stage.\", \"BAdam is interpreted as a block-wise Adam: at each step one parameter block receives an Adam-style update while remaining blocks are frozen; the active block rotates over a schedule (contiguous partition or V-BAdam random schedule). Source: assumed from general recollection of 'BAdam: A Memory-Efficient Full-Parameter Optimization of Large Language Models' \\u2014 NOT verified from primary source in this workspace.\", \"Per-step 'learning perturbation' is the parameter-difference \\u0394\\u03b8_t = \\u03b8_{t+1} \\u2212 \\u03b8_t at the optimizer boundary (post-step), not the raw gradient and not the post-LR-scaled direction.\", \"'Heavy-tailed singular value distribution' is operationalised as a Pareto(\\u03b1) fit on the upper tail with \\u03b1 estimated by Hill estimator and a KS goodness-of-fit; a heavy tail is positive if \\u03b1 \\u2208 (0, 2] (variance possibly infinite) AND Marchenko\\u2013Pastur reference is rejected.\", \"'Effective rank' defaults to Roy & Vetterli (2007); numerical-rank @ \\u03b5 is a secondary cross-check.\", \"Comparable-by-default thresholds \\u03c4_e = 0.20 and d_e = 0.30 are PLACEHOLDERS, to be pre-registered with the researcher at the result stage.\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"Exact BAdam update rule, default block size, LR scaling, and state-allocation strategy are assumed, not source-confirmed.\", \"Whether the sandbox will allow execution at all (no GPU, no installed ML stack, no network); this prototype of the design accommodates that by being deliverable as a design protocol.\", \"Whether task.json's referenced track.md carries additional scoping constraints that I cannot see here.\", \"Whether 'heavy-tailed' admits \\u03b1 > 2 in this paper's convention is unknown; threshold to be agreed.\", \"Whether the per-step or per-cycle \\u0394W is the right primary endpoint for comparing erank is a definitional call, not a statistical one.\"]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-cbe18d2d-8a12-4cf5-a924-87d3d935627e", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 16}
